From 7a67452976b1cd645008d3fc7d07cd45f3e20642 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Halo <halo@localhost>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 13:10:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Halo: time-based widget animation engine

Replace the frame-stepped, move-only eWidgetAnimation with a timer-driven
engine that moves a widget over a fixed duration with an easing curve
(linear, ease-out cubic, ease-in-out cubic, ease-out back). Frames are
computed from the monotonic clock, so slow frames skip ahead instead of
stretching the animation, and it works in immediate and buffered
composition modes.

Expose eWidget.animateMove(), stopAnimation() and isAnimating() to Python.

Add an opt-in switch for the buffered compositor: create
/etc/enigma2/halo-buffered or set HALO_BUFFERED=1 before starting enigma2.
